86	1359	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>A single misconfigured laptop can provide an entry point for an entire network. Hardening involves turning off unnecessary services, enforcing disk encryption, and ensuring OS patches are up to date.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Neozaar provides a structured approach to endpoint hardening based on industry standards (CIS Benchmarks). We automate the enforcement of security policies across your fleet, ensuring that every device—regardless of OS—meets a "Gold Standard" of security before it can access corporate data.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Our service covers the complete lifecycle of endpoint configuration and compliance:&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Baseline Design: Design of security baselines for Windows, macOS, and Linux based on CIS Benchmarks.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Assessment: Vulnerability assessment of the entire endpoint fleet to identify gaps.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Policy Enforcement: Implementation of hardening policies via MDM (Mobile Device Management) or RMM (Remote Monitoring and Management) tools.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Privilege Management: Removal of local admin rights and management of user privileges.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Application Control: Implementation of application whitelisting to prevent unauthorized software execution.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Neozaar utilizes a "Zero Trust" methodology to secure the device layer:&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 1: Audit &amp; Align: We audit your current configurations and align them with CIS Benchmarks to create a secure baseline.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 2: Automate: We automate patch management for OS and 3rd party apps to eliminate vulnerability windows.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 3: Control: We enforce strict controls on peripherals/USB ports and manage Full Disk Encryption (FDE) to prevent physical data theft.&nbsp;</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	["Reduced Attack Surface: Significant reduction in the attack surface by eliminating unnecessary services and privileges. ","Compliance Readiness: Automated compliance reporting ready for SOC2/HIPAA or internal auditors. ","Operational Consistency: Standardization of security settings across a fragmented device fleet. ","Data Protection: Prevention of data theft via removable media and unencrypted drives. ","Proactive Defense: A shift from reactive incident response to proactive vulnerability management by fixing root causes. "]	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Vulnerabilities: Elimination of risks from unpatched software vulnerabilities.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Inconsistency: Resolving inconsistent security settings across different devices and OS versions.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Data Leakage: Mitigating data theft risks via removable media (USB drives).&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Privilege Abuse: Reducing risks associated with users holding unnecessary local admin privileges.&nbsp;</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>			[]	2026-02-26 10:10:25.016	2026-07-24 12:44:48.455
