1360	401	Zero Trust Network Access ZTNA Migration 	Replacing traditional broad-access VPNs with granular, identity-based access controls that enforce least privilege, continuous verification, and secure connectivity to critical applications.	Traditional VPNs give users "the keys to the kingdom" once they are inside the network, which is a major risk if a device is compromised. Shift your strategy from "connect then verify" to "verify then connect." \r\n\r\nUsing Sophos ZTNA and Check Point Harmony Connect, Neozaar helps you transition to a Zero Trust architecture. We move your users from broad network-level access to specific, application-level access based on their identity and device health, significantly reducing the lateral movement risk.	["Identity-aware access control (seamless MFA integration) ","Device health checks before connection (Posture Check) ","Elimination of the \\"VPN Bottleneck\\" for cloud apps ","Micro-segmentation of internal resources ","Improved end-user experience with transparent connectivity "]	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Securing a 100% remote or hybrid workforce&nbsp;</span></li><li>Providing secure access for contractors and third parties&nbsp;</li><li>Replacing end-of-life VPN hardware&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	{CISO,"Network Lead",CIO,"IAM Lead"}	{"Identity & Access Security"}	{AWS,Azure,GCP}	{Global}	{"Request a Demo"}	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Integration with Identity Providers (Azure AD, Okta, etc.)&nbsp;</span></li><li>Visibility into application hosting environments&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><div><br></div><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	One Time	\N	\N	\N	NEO-2026-1098		https://neoblob.blob.core.windows.net/neoblobcontainer/1784896416134_1221_Neozaar_Zero_Trust_Network_Access_(ZTNA)_Migration.jpg	{https://neoblob.blob.core.windows.net/neoblobcontainer/1786006949413_8513_Zero_Trust_Network_Access_(ZTNA)_Migration_(1)_(1).png}	{"https://neoblob.blob.core.windows.net/neoblobcontainer/Ne