1521	401	Multi-Region Continuity & Autonomous Failover Architecture	Business continuity solution enabling autonomous multi-region failover, ensuring critical applications stay available and recover automatically during failures and disruptions.	Modern enterprises depend on highly available infrastructure, yet regional outages, cyber incidents, or infrastructure failures can disrupt critical services. The Neozaar Multi-Region Continuity & Autonomous Failover Architecture is a solution designed to ensure continuous service availability by distributing workloads and recovery capabilities across multiple geographic regions. By implementing automated failover mechanisms, dependency-aware recovery sequencing, and continuous health monitoring, the architecture enables systems to shift operations seamlessly when disruptions occur. This solution helps organizations maintain operational continuity, reduce downtime, and ensure critical workloads remain accessible even during major regional disruptions.	["Multi-region workload resilience architecture","Autonomous failover orchestration","Continuous infrastructure health monitoring","Application dependency-aware recovery sequencing","Automated failback and restoration processes"]	<ul><li><span>Multi-region\r\ndisaster recovery architecture</span></li><li><span>Continuous application availability strategy</span></li><li><span>Regional outage resilience planning</span></li><li><span>Enterprise business continuity implementation</span></li></ul><p style=" margin: 0"></p>	{CISO,"IT Head","Network Lead",CTO}	{"Disaster Recovery","Operational Resilience"}	{AWS,Azure,GCP}	{Global}	{"Request for Demo"}	<p class="MsoNormal">Multi-region infrastructure deployment capabilities<br>\r\nAccess to backup, monitoring, and disaster recovery orchestration platforms<br>\r\nVisibility into application dependencies and infrastructure configurations</p><p style=" margin: 0"></p>	One Time	\N	\N	\N	NEO-2026-1220		https://neozaarassets.blob.core.windows