1295	401	Identity Threat Detection and Response ITDR	Continuous monitoring of identity activities to detect, investigate, and automatically contain credential abuse, privilege misuse, and account hijacking attempts in real time. \r\n	While IAM prevents unauthorized access, ITDR detects when a legitimate identity is being misused. Attackers often steal tokens or use sophisticated phishing to bypass MFA. This solution uses behavioral AI to establish a "normal" baseline for every user. If a user suddenly logs in from an implausible location or begins downloading massive amounts of data, Neozaar’s ITDR automatically triggers containment actions—such as killing the session or requiring a biometric re-authentication—stopping the breach in its tracks.	["Behavioral Anomaly Detection","Automated Containment","Token Theft Protection","Real-Time Policy Enforcement","Attack Path Visualization"]	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Detecting compromised user accounts in real-time.&nbsp;</span></li><li>Preventing data exfiltration by insiders.&nbsp;</li><li>protecting against sophisticated ransomware that uses valid credentials.</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	{CISO,"SOC Lead","IAM Lead","IT Head"}	{"Identity & Access Security"}	{AWS,Azure,GCP,IBM}	{Global}	{"Request a Demo"}	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Audit logs enabled on Identity Providers (IdPs).&nbsp;</span></li><li>API access to Cloud Identity Management systems.&nbsp;</li><li>Baseline of normal user activity (requires learning period).</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	One Time	\N	\N	\N	NEO-2026-1069		https://neoblob.blob.core.windows.net/neoblobcontainer/1784896483948_5978_Neozaar_Identity_Threat_Detection_Response_(ITDR).jpg	{https://neoblob.blob.core.windows.net/neoblobcontainer/1786007740075_7966_Identity_Threat_Detection_&_Response_(ITDR).png}	{"https://neoblob.blob.core.windows.net/neoblobcontainer/Neozaar Identity Threat Detection & Response (ITDR) Solution.pdf"}		{"https://